A savory, sweet, and smoky barbecue-inspired chili made easy in the slow cooker or on the stovetop. Features three kinds of beans and tender shredded chicken breasts infused with liquid smoke, smoked paprika, and Worcestershire.

*Adapted from [Carlsbad Cravings](https://carlsbadcravings.com/smoky-bbq-chicken-chili-slow-cooker-stove-top/).*

## Ingredients

- 1 pound boneless, skinless chicken breasts
- 1 tablespoon olive oil
- 4 garlic cloves, minced
- 1 small onion, finely chopped
- ½ cup ketchup
- 3 tablespoons brown sugar
- 2 teaspoons yellow mustard
- 2 tablespoons apple cider vinegar
- 2 tablespoons Worcestershire sauce
- 1 can (16 oz) cannellini beans, undrained
- 1 can (14 oz) kidney beans, undrained
- 1 can (14 oz) pinto beans, undrained
- 1 can (4 oz) mild diced green chilies
- 2 teaspoons liquid smoke
- 2 teaspoons chili powder
- 1 teaspoon ground cumin
- 1 teaspoon smoked paprika
- 1 teaspoon kosher salt
- ½ teaspoon freshly ground black pepper
- 1 can (14.5 oz) low-sodium chicken broth whisked with 1 tablespoon cornstarch
- Hot sauce, to taste (added at the end)

## Instructions

1. **Layer the Slow Cooker:** Rub chicken breasts with olive oil and lay them in the bottom of the slow cooker. Add all remaining ingredients—except the hot sauce—and stir the liquid and beans around the chicken breasts.
2. **Cook Until Tender:** Cover and cook on LOW for 6 to 8 hours or on HIGH for 3 to 4 hours, until the chicken is tender and pulls apart easily.
3. **Shred the Chicken:** Remove the chicken breasts to a cutting board and shred with two forks (or dice into bite-sized pieces). Return the chicken to the slow cooker and cook on LOW for an additional 20 minutes to allow the meat to absorb the chili flavors.
4. **Season and Serve:** Stir in hot sauce to taste. If you prefer a thinner consistency, stir in an extra splash of warm water or chicken broth. Ladle into bowls and serve with your favorite chili toppings.

## Notes

- **Stovetop Instructions:** Heat 1 tablespoon olive oil in a large Dutch oven over medium heat. Sauté the chopped onion and garlic for 3–4 minutes until softened. Add the whole chicken breasts, beans with liquid, green chilies, ketchup, brown sugar, mustard, vinegar, Worcestershire, seasonings, and broth whisked with cornstarch. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to low, cover, and gently simmer for 45 to 60 minutes until the chicken shreds easily. Shred the chicken, return to the pot, and simmer uncovered 10 minutes to thicken.
- **Serving Suggestions:** Top with shredded sharp cheddar cheese, a dollop of sour cream, sliced green onions, and crushed tortilla chips or warm cornbread.
